/** @mainpage Qore git Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section gitintro Git Module Introduction

    The \c git module provides a comprehensive interface to git repositories from
    %Qore using the libgit2 library. It supports all common git operations including
    repository management, staging, committing, branching, tagging, diffing, merging,
    and remote operations.

    This module is released under the MIT license (see \c COPYING.MIT in the source
    distribution for more information). The module is tagged as such in the module's
    header (meaning it can be loaded unconditionally regardless of how the %Qore
    library was initialized).

    To use this module, use \c "%requires git" in your code.

    @section gitrequirements Requirements

    This module requires:
    - libgit2 >= 1.0
    - %Qore >= 2.0

    @section gitclasses Classes Provided

    The following classes are provided by this module:
    - @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository "GitRepository": main class for interacting with git repositories

    @section gitexamples Examples

    @par Example: Initialize a repository and create a commit
    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires git

# initialize a new repo
GitRepository repo = GitRepository::init("/tmp/test-repo");
repo.configSet("user.name", "Test User");
repo.configSet("user.email", "test@example.com");

# create a file and commit
File f();
f.open(repo.workdir() + "hello.txt", O_CREAT | O_WRONLY | O_TRUNC);
f.write("Hello, World!\n");
f.close();

repo.add("hello.txt");
string oid = repo.commit("Initial commit");
printf("Commit: %s\n", oid);
    @endcode

    @section gitreleasenotes Release Notes

    @subsection git_1_0 git Module Version 1.0
    - initial release
*/
